  "articleBody": "Getting arrested for a drug crime can be super overwhelming, and it's totally normal to feel lost about what comes next. Knowing the general process can help you feel a little more prepared. First, you'll likely go through booking, where your information is recorded, and then you might be held for questioning. This is a critical time, and you have the right to remain silent and to speak with an attorney. After booking, a bail hearing might be set, or you could be released on your own recognizance depending on the charges. Then, the formal legal process kicks off, often with an arraignment where you'll hear the charges against you and enter a plea. Don't go through this alone. Having an experienced attorney like Angelo Reyes by your side from the very beginning is crucial. We can navigate the complexities of the San Diego legal system, ensure your rights are protected, and work towards the best possible outcome for your situation. Waiting can make things more complicated, so getting professional help quickly is always a smart move.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
}